From:=?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Valentin?= <avalentin@marcant.net>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Report the station RSNXE in STA info

The RSN Extension element a station sent is kept in the WPA state machine
for the whole association, but it is not reported anywhere. Add it as an
rsnxe field to the STA info of the control interface, hex encoded.

The element answers what a station can do rather than what it did: SAE
hash-to-element, SAE-PK, protected TWT, secure LTF and secure RTT all
live in its capability bits. Without it the only way to tell whether a
station supports SAE-PK is to switch SAE-PK on and see who stops
connecting.

It is reported as raw hex rather than decoded flags on purpose. The bit
assignments keep growing, and a management system can decode what it
knows and keep the rest, while a decoded string would have to be taught
every new bit here first.

Signed-off-by:=?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Valentin?= <avalentin@marcant.net>
---
diff --git a/src/ap/wpa_auth.c b/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
@@ -6742,6 +6742,15 @@
 }
 
 
+const u8 * wpa_auth_get_rsnxe(struct wpa_state_machine *sm, size_t *len)
+{
+	if (!sm || !sm->rsnxe || !sm->rsnxe_len)
+		return NULL;
+	*len = sm->rsnxe_len;
+	return sm->rsnxe;
+}
+
+
 int wpa_auth_sta_key_mgmt(struct wpa_state_machine *sm)
 {
 	if (!sm)
diff --git a/src/ap/wpa_auth.h b/src/ap/wpa_auth.h
--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth.h
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth.h
@@ -512,6 +512,7 @@
 int wpa_auth_get_pairwise(struct wpa_state_machine *sm);
 const u8 * wpa_auth_get_pmk(struct wpa_state_machine *sm, int *len);
 const u8 * wpa_auth_get_dpp_pkhash(struct wpa_state_machine *sm);
+const u8 * wpa_auth_get_rsnxe(struct wpa_state_machine *sm, size_t *len);
 int wpa_auth_sta_key_mgmt(struct wpa_state_machine *sm);
 bool wpa_auth_get_first_sta_seen(struct wpa_authenticator *wpa_auth,
 				 int vlan_id);
diff --git a/src/ap/ctrl_iface_ap.c b/src/ap/ctrl_iface_ap.c
--- a/src/ap/ctrl_iface_ap.c
+++ b/src/ap/ctrl_iface_ap.c
@@ -500,6 +500,22 @@
 			len += ret;
 	}
 
+	{
+		size_t rsnxe_len;
+		const u8 *rsnxe = wpa_auth_get_rsnxe(sta->wpa_sm, &rsnxe_len);
+
+		if (rsnxe) {
+			ret = os_snprintf(buf + len, buflen - len, "rsnxe=");
+			if (!os_snprintf_error(buflen - len, ret))
+				len += ret;
+			len += wpa_snprintf_hex(buf + len, buflen - len,
+						rsnxe, rsnxe_len);
+			ret = os_snprintf(buf + len, buflen - len, "\n");
+			if (!os_snprintf_error(buflen - len, ret))
+				len += ret;
+		}
+	}
+
 	dpp_pkhash = ap_sta_wpa_get_dpp_pkhash(hapd, sta);
 	if (dpp_pkhash) {
 		ret = os_snprintf(buf + len, buflen - len, "dpp_pkhash=");
